{
  "proto_version": "0.7.0",
  "$comment": "Cencora NDC2's flow scope (customer/cencora/site/ndc2/flow): putaway and pick through the relay racking, the L-Shape template's flow over Cencora's 16 put stations, 10 pick stations and 19 aisles, so that a Studio run of the site needs no launch line. Each quantity a run reads is the one Dematic's Scenario 13 ran with (its spec, libs/dessim/tests/fixtures/cencora_v3_da50_scenario13_spec.json, which `main` does not carry but the delivery branch wip/dematic-batch-13-14 does at a12eec2ce, and its launch line) but three, each standing in for what this tree does not have. The put stations' 261.4 presentations an hour is Scenario 5's (sim/dessim/tests/fixtures/cencora_v3_da50_scenario5_spec.json), since in Scenario 13 each put station's operator paced induction. The pick stations' 6.77 s pick is Scenario 5's operator time; Scenario 13's spec carries it too, but there the operator each pick station's world states, the Mujin arm, timed every pick. Their sequencing is `sequenced`, standing in for Scenario 13's `strict`. Neither `strict`, nor one pallet at a time, nor stations worked by their operators, nor the uncrossed draw of random slots is stated, since this tree does not have them. Scenario 13's launch line set putaway.random_slots_uncrossed, which draws a deposit's random relay among those a DA50 can serve without crossing the other DA50 on its aisle's shared rail, and among all the candidates when there is none; this run always draws among all the candidates. The map states each station's operator, and nothing on this tree reads it.",
